1
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,540
Hey, guys.

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,540
Hey.

3
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,130
Hi.

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,130
Hey.

5
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:09,170
Uh, we need to talk about something.

6
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:12,300
Yeah. We don't feel like we can host Thanksgiving this year.

7
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,130
What?

8
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,130
Are you kidding?

9
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,090
Well, it's just with work and the stress of adoption...

10
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:19,180
...we don't feel like we have the energy.

11
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:23,350
Plus, we don't think it's fair that every year the burden falls on us.

12
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,560
That doesn't sound like you.

13
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:29,360
That's Monica talking.

14
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:33,940
No, no. We made this decision together.

15
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:36,280
She's putting words in your mouth.

16
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:40,080
Don't you put words in people's mouths. You put turkey in people's mouths.

17
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,710
I can't believe this. This is Emma's first Thanksgiving.

18
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:49,080
No, it's not.

19
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:49,080
It's not? When was she born?

20
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:53,760
Well, personally, I think it's great you're giving yourself a break.

21
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,590
Thank you, Pheebs.

22
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,590
Sure. It's just as well.

23
00:00:56,760 --> 00:01:00,600
I mean, last year wasn't very good. I think she's losing her touch.

24
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,980
What? You are way off, lady.

25
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,980
Am I? Really? Am I?

26
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:08,690
Well, why don't you cook Thanksgiving dinner and prove me wrong.

27
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:13,440
Well, think about it. You'd be trying to top what you did last year.

28
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:16,820
You'd be in competition with yourself.

29
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,990
That's my favorite kind.

30
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,910
Okay, we are doing this.

31
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,160
Don't let yourself get manipulated this way.

32
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:29,040
Stay out of this, Chandler. This is between me and me.

33
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:34,090
We are supposed to make these decisions together.

34
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:37,380
Did you not watch the Dr. Phil I taped for you?

35
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,110
Hey.

36
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:34,110
Hi. Happy Thanksgiving.

37
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:36,610
Oh, yeah. Happy Meatless Turkey-Murder Day.

38
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:41,240
You guys, I ordered some chocolate pies from that bakery on Bleeker.

39
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:44,160
Could you pick them up for me?

40
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:44,160
You're not making the pies?

41
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:45,870
No, I don't make chocolate pies.

42
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,580
When I was younger, I entered this pie-eating contest.

43
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:51,370
I ate so many that the thought of them makes me sick.

44
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,250
Did you at least win the contest?

45
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,550
Two minutes, twelve pies and a part of one tin.

46
00:02:57,710 --> 00:03:00,340
Okay, I'll see you guys at 4.

47
00:02:57,710 --> 00:03:00,340
Can't wait.

48
00:03:00,510 --> 00:03:05,390
This dinner is gonna be so great. In your face, last-year me.

49
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:07,930
Hey, Rach?

50
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:07,930
Yeah.

51
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,770
Um, what's Emma doing today?

52
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:13,730
Well, let's see, uh, I know that she has a meeting with her lawyer...

53
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:17,520
...and then she has to make a very big poop.

54
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,610
Why?

55
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,610
Well, I want to enter her...

56
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:22,400
...in a baby beauty pageant.

57
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:26,660
Oh, my God. That's the creepiest thing I've ever heard.

58
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:30,080
Okay, but before you say no, my friend Suzanne is entering her kid.

59
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:32,620
And compared to Emma, she's a real dog.

60
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:36,750
Agh. Phoebe, all babies are beautiful.

61
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:36,750
Oh, okay.

62
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:41,170
No. Ugh, Phoebe, just the idea of pitting one baby against another...

63
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:44,590
...I mean, you know, and judging who's cuter just for a trophy...

64
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:48,680
And a thousand dollars. ...is something I'm very interested in.

65
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:52,430
Oh, please, do not tell Ross.

66
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:55,310
He still believes that what's on the inside is important.

67
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:59,480
Okay. Oh, and Emma needs a cowgirl outfit for the competition.

68
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:02,400
Where am I gonna get a cowgirl outfit on Thanksgiving?

69
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:04,570
Well, I was thinking...

70
00:04:02,570 --> 00:04:04,570
Take the clothes...

71
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,280
...off Joey's Cabbage Patch Kid!

72
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:07,280
Yeah!

73
00:04:16,170 --> 00:04:17,960
Did someone drop the baton again?

74
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:21,590
Why come all the way from Kansas to do that?

75
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:27,590
I don't get older, I just get better.

76
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,890
You know what just occurred to me?

77
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,680
This could be our last Thanksgiving just the two of us.

78
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:35,020
I mean, we could be getting a baby soon.

79
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:37,650
You don't know that.

80
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:37,650
Somebody's gonna pick us.

81
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:40,650
But we haven't heard a thing from the adoption agency.

82
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:42,860
I'm telling you, it's gonna happen.

83
00:04:43,030 --> 00:04:47,160
Next year, it's gonna be you, me and little Hemingway Bing.

84
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:51,830
What? He's my favorite author.

85
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:51,830
Name one of his books.

86
00:04:57,750 --> 00:04:59,290
The Firm?

87
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:04,210
Okay, let's see. Okay, the turkey's in the oven. The stuffing is ready.

88
00:05:04,380 --> 00:05:08,550
You know, you always cook this meal all by yourself. Let me help this year.

89
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,350
Oh, Chandler, that's sweet.

90
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:13,430
But you don't have to do everything Dr. Phil tells you to do.

91
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:19,810
I'm serious, let me do something. Just not the turkey. Nothing high-profile.

92
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:22,520
Okay, let's see. Oh, the cranberry sauce.

93
00:05:22,690 --> 00:05:25,690
It's easy to make, and no one really cares about it.

94
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:28,030
Tell me more.

95
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:32,870
I'm gonna go check on something across the hall. You start by washing these.

96
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:36,910
Not with soap!

97
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:44,590
You obviously haven't tasted my Palmolive potatoes.

98
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:49,760
Hi. Hey, guess what Joey has.

99
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:49,760
Three tickets to today's Rangers game!

100
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:52,720
Dude, I wanted him to guess.

101
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:52,720
Oh.

102
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:55,430
Oh, my God.

103
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:55,430
Yeah, they're great seats too.

104
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,480
Guess where they are.

105
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,480
Center ice.

106
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,560
Did I do something to you?

107
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,940
Mm. The game's at 1.

108
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,940
So?

109
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:09,990
Dinner's at 4. We'll never make it back.

110
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:09,990
We leave before it's over. We'll be back.

111
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,950
You say that, but it could take us a long time to get home.

112
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:17,330
Plus, Joey could get lost and they could have to page us to go pick him up.

113
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:20,790
Dude, two times that happened!

114
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,460
Look, Monica's been working hard all day.

115
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:27,420
She didn't want to host in the first place. We shouldn't go.

116
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:29,130
He's right, man.

117
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:32,140
Yeah, I guess. So we'll see you at 4.

118
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:32,140
Okay.

119
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,350
And get ready to taste my very special cranberries.

120
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,890
Or should I say "Chan-berries"?

121
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:45,480
That's some gentle comedy, dude.

122
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,980
We're still going to the game.

123
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:49,950
Yeah.

124
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:49,950
Yeah.

125
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:57,910
This is contestant number 16, Rebecca Hope from Yonkers.

126
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,120
Hey.

127
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,120
Phoebe, listen, I think we gotta go.

128
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:01,670
This place is freaking me out.

129
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:05,500
I've been watching this guy over there. I don't think he came with a kid.

130
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,090
But we can't leave now.

131
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,880
There was this one baby, Haley, who was favored to win...

132
00:07:10,050 --> 00:07:11,970
...she got croup, so she had to stay home.

133
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,970
This competition just blew wide-open, folks.

134
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,760
Phoebe, it's just too weird.

135
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:20,430
I just saw a 1 -year-old run around with pantyhose on.

136
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,520
Oh, I know. We should've been more prepared.

137
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:28,860
It's okay. Now, the way I see it, our real competition now is Cameron.

138
00:07:29,030 --> 00:07:30,990
My God, they just took her sweater off.

139
00:07:31,150 --> 00:07:33,360
Look at those arms. Hello, Michelin Man.

140
00:07:33,530 --> 00:07:34,700
Oh, Phoebe.

141
00:07:33,530 --> 00:07:34,700
Whoo-hoo.

142
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:37,410
Come on! You know what, it's already 3:00.

143
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:40,700
They haven't even gotten to Emma's group yet. We got dinner.

144
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:43,870
But Emma's got what it takes. She could go all the way!

145
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:50,050
Phoebe, you have to calm down.

146
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:50,050
Ahem. Okay.

147
00:07:50,210 --> 00:07:55,590
Rachel, the hottest babies in the tri-state area are in this room right now.

148
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:01,350
I overheard one judge say that not one of them holds a candle to Emma.

149
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,930
Really?

150
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,930
Yeah.

151
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,730
You heard him say that?

152
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,730
Yeah.

153
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:10,030
All right. Okay. All right, let's give these babies something to cry about.

154
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:14,030
Good. Let's get down to business. Emma needs some makeup.

155
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,450
What? No... What?

156
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,870
She's gonna look washed-out next to the others.

157
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:20,450
No, I'm not letting you put makeup on my baby.

158
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,870
Why not?

159
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,870
Because I already did.

160
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:33,420
Oh! You bum! Get off the ice!

161
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:33,420
You suck! Get off the ice, you idiot!

162
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,340
What a game.

163
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,340
I know. Yeah.

164
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:40,850
I can't believe Chandler's missing this.

165
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:40,850
I'm sorry he's not here.

166
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:45,020
But I gotta say, I am really enjoying nacho chair.

167
00:08:45,190 --> 00:08:48,690
Yeah, I'd probably enjoy it more if you didn't keep batting my hand away.

168
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:51,150
Oh!

169
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,940
Yeah!

170
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,940
These seats are great.

171
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:56,110
I know, I know. When I was here for "Holidays on Ice"...

172
00:08:57,820 --> 00:09:02,290
...I was sitting so far away, Michelle Kwan couldn't read my banner.

173
00:09:02,790 --> 00:09:06,040
Whoa, we'd better get going. If we don't leave now, we're gonna be late.

174
00:09:06,210 --> 00:09:09,790
But it's a tie game. So we're a little late. The girls will be there.

175
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,090
Let's just stay for one more goal.

176
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,760
I don't know.

177
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,760
One more fight.

178
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,880
Okay.

179
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,880
Okay.

180
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,890
Where is everybody? They're 45 minutes late.

181
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:27,140
I can't believe they're not here. I slave and I slave for what?

182
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:29,270
They've ruined Cranberry Day.

183
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,820
How late are we?

184
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,820
Forty-five minutes.

185
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:35,030
Wow.

186
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:35,030
Here.

187
00:09:35,190 --> 00:09:36,440
Yeah. Okay.

188
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:40,320
Rachel and Phoebe are already there, so they probably started without us.

189
00:09:40,490 --> 00:09:43,870
We could just slip in, and no one needs to know where we were.

190
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:49,120
You may want to lose the foam finger.

191
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:49,120
Oh, no, no, no.

192
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:50,750
You just want to put it on your hand.

193
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,800
Hey.

194
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,800
Oh.

195
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,800
You...? You're not at Thanksgiving?

196
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:58,800
No.

197
00:09:56,970 --> 00:09:58,800
No, we're late.

198
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:01,260
What are you doing here?

199
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:01,260
We're late too.

200
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,220
We figured we could be late because you'd be on time.

201
00:10:05,390 --> 00:10:08,690
Don't point that thing at me, Tribbiani.

202
00:10:08,850 --> 00:10:12,110
Nobody's here? Monica's gonna kill us.

203
00:10:08,850 --> 00:10:12,110
Yeah, where were you?

204
00:10:12,270 --> 00:10:14,480
Well... Uh...

205
00:10:12,270 --> 00:10:14,480
Yeah, what's with the trophy?

206
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:18,360
Uh, well, uh...

207
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:18,360
We were at a spelling bee.

208
00:10:19,610 --> 00:10:21,320
And I won.

209
00:10:22,070 --> 00:10:26,080
You won an adult Thanksgiving Day spelling bee?

210
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:29,870
Yes. Y-E-S. Yes.

211
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,710
Let me see this.

212
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:35,420
"Grand Supreme Little Darling, New York Division"?

213
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:38,050
That's me. Heh.

214
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:42,680
You entered Emma in a beauty pageant?

215
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:46,850
And it looks like she put makeup on her.

216
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:51,190
Wait a second. Where have I seen that cowgirl outfit before?

217
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:54,770
I can't believe this. She's our daughter.

218
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,650
That you would treat her like some kind of show dog is inexcusable.

219
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:02,860
She won a thousand dollars.

220
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:02,860
So this is an annual thing?

221
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:09,410
That's Alicia May Emory's outfit!

222
00:11:10,830 --> 00:11:13,880
Guys, there are people in there who are not getting any happier.

223
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,000
What are we gonna do?

224
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,000
Figure it out.

225
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:17,710
I gotta put Emma down for a nap.

226
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:21,050
And, Rach, while you're in there, throw something on Alicia May.

227
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:25,180
All right, what are we gonna say?

228
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:25,180
Ooh!

229
00:11:25,350 --> 00:11:27,060
We'll say that we were mugged.

230
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:29,720
You can't get mad at someone who's been mugged.

231
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:32,060
Good. But you don't look like you were mugged.

232
00:11:32,230 --> 00:11:34,520
No. Here.

233
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,440
Hey!

234
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,950
Do you hear something?

235
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:49,240
They're out there.

236
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:51,830
Let me see.

237
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,250
I can't believe this. They're an hour late...

238
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:58,000
...and they're just standing out there talking.

239
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:03,430
Everything's so distorted. It looks like Joey has a giant hand.

240
00:12:04,970 --> 00:12:07,390
That says "Rangers" on it. They went to the game.

241
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:11,770
Oh, they are in for a world of pain.

242
00:12:13,810 --> 00:12:17,810
Ross' shirt is torn.

243
00:12:13,810 --> 00:12:17,810
They're late and they're sloppy.

244
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,440
All right, Emma's napping. What happened to your shirt?

245
00:12:22,610 --> 00:12:26,450
I got mugged, and they stole my pocket.

246
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:30,580
We're just trying to figure out an excuse.

247
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:33,040
Hey, ooh! How about this?

248
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:37,580
We could say that Monica told us 5:00, not 4:00. That way we're right on time.

249
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:39,210
Or!

250
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:44,010
Or we could plant PCP in the apartment and call the cops on her.

251
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:50,260
That would be a good way to get rid of all the PCP we have lying around.

252
00:12:50,430 --> 00:12:52,390
We'll just say that she said it was 5:00.

253
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:55,310
We'll just act casual. We're not late, we're right on time.

254
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:02,860
"We know you're out there."

255
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,200
Who do you think it's from?

256
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:20,290
Oh, God, this is bad. This is so bad.

257
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:22,800
Well, let's just go in there and face them.

258
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:28,130
